  "title": "China and EU reach landmark deal to halve hybrid car exports",
  "summary": "Brussels and Beijing agreed to a landmark deal to halve hybrid car exports to the EU, aiming to curb European job losses and address trade tensions. The deal marks the first of its kind and resulted from intense negotiations since June.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "China and the EU agreed to halve hybrid car exports over four years, with the EU aiming to reduce sales by more than half.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The deal was reached after a series of negotiations between the two economies, with the EU citing concerns over rising European car industry sales.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EU’s trade commissioner confirmed the deal was the first of its kind and resulted from “intense” negotiations with China.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
